### Firmware (required, built locally)

The firmware package is **not** in the GitHub release: NVIDIA's license does not clearly allow redistributing the
blobs, so the plugin downloads the pinned 610.43.03 inputs from NVIDIA/CachyOS on this machine, verifies their
SHA-256, and builds the package locally. It needs `python3`, `zstd`, about 1 GB of free space and several minutes.

<form markdown="1" method="POST" action="/update.php" target="progressFrame">
<input type="hidden" name="#command" value="/plugins/<?=$plugin?>/scripts/gpu-turing-unlock">
<input type="hidden" name="#arg[1]" value="firmware">
: <input type="submit" value="Build firmware package">
</form>

> After it finishes, reboot so the module loads with the firmware in place.

